.TH CLAUDE-WAKER 1 "2026-08-04" "claude-waker 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude\-waker \- keep Claude Code sessions in iTerm2 awake on a schedule
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude\-waker
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude\-waker
periodically types a message into iTerm2 sessions whose name matches a pattern.
It exists so that Claude Code sessions which have stopped and are waiting for
input can be told to
.B continue
while you are away.
.PP
Run with no arguments on a terminal it presents an interactive menu. Given any
flag or subcommand it runs non\-interactively, so it is equally at home in a
script or a cron entry. The subcommand may appear before or after the flags.
.PP
It talks to iTerm2 through
.BR osascript (1)
and has no other dependencies. It will not launch iTerm2; if iTerm2 is not
running it exits 3.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the wake loop.
.TP
.B menu
Force the interactive menu.
.TP
.B list
List the current iTerm2 sessions with their tty and state.
.TP
.B status
Show the resolved settings and which sessions currently match, then exit
without sending anything.
.TP
.B install\-plugin
Install a "Claude Waker" entry into iTerm2's Scripts menu.
.TP
.B config
Show the config file path and the effective settings.
.TP
.B version ", " help
Print the version or the usage summary.
.SH TARGETING
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-match " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Match sessions by name. Default
.BR dev3 .
Because the default mode is a substring match, this keeps working as Claude Code
rewrites the session title.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-match\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
One of
.BR contains " (default), " exact ", " glob ", " regex .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Match case\-insensitively.
.TP
.BR \-\-session\-id " " \fIUUID\fR
Target one exact session. Repeatable. Survives renames.
.TP
.BR \-\-tty " " \fIDEV\fR
Target by tty. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Target every session.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Skip sessions whose name contains \fIPATTERN\fR. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-first
Only the first match.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-match
Exit non\-zero instead of warning when nothing matches.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-targets " " \fIN\fR
Refuse to run if more than \fIN\fR sessions match.
.SH MESSAGE
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text " " \fISTR\fR
The text to type. Default
.BR continue .
Repeat the flag to rotate between several messages across iterations.
.TP
.BR \-\-text\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read the message from a file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-newline
Type the text without pressing Enter.
.TP
.B \-\-esc\-first
Send Escape before the text, clearing any half\-typed line.
.PP
The message is passed to AppleScript as an argument rather than interpolated
into the script source, so quotes, backslashes and
.B $(...)
arrive verbatim and are never evaluated.
.SH SCHEDULE
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
How many sends. Default 16.
.B 0
means no limit.
.TP
.B \-\-forever
Same as
.BR "\-\-count 0" .
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-every " " \fIDUR\fR
Gap between sends. Default
.BR 45m .
.TP
.BR \-\-jitter " " \fIDUR\fR|\fIN\fB%\fR
Randomise each gap by plus or minus this much.
.TP
.BR \-\-delay " " \fIDUR\fR
Wait before the first send.
.TP
.BR \-\-at " " \fIHH:MM\fR
Make the first send at a wall\-clock time.
.TP
.BR \-\-until " " \fIHH:MM\fR
Stop sending after this time.
.TP
.BR \-\-deadline " " \fIDUR\fR
Stop after this much elapsed time.
.TP
.B \-\-legacy\-timing
Reproduce the asymmetric sleep of the original shell loop, which slept only for
the first half of its iterations.
.PP
Durations are plain seconds
.RB ( 2700 )
or unit strings:
.BR 90s ", " 45m ", " 1h30m ", " 2d .
There are \fIN\-1\fR waits for \fIN\fR sends; nothing sleeps after the last one.
.SH GUARDS
.TP
.B \-\-if\-idle
Skip sessions that are streaming output at that moment. This maps onto iTerm2's
.B is processing
property, which is true while Claude is producing an answer and false while it
waits for input. Note that a session blocked on a silent command, such as
.BR sleep ,
also reads as idle because nothing is being written to the terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-if\-prompt
Only send when the session is at a shell prompt. Requires iTerm2 shell
integration; without it no session appears to be at a prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-if\-gone
Exit when a targeted session disappears.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would happen and send nothing. Waits are not actually slept.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Errors only.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Extra detail, including session ids in
.BR list .
.TP
.BR \-\-log " " \fIFILE\fR
Append a timestamped record of every send.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Post a macOS notification on each wake.
.TP
.BR \-\-countdown ", " \-\-no\-countdown
Force the live countdown on or off. It is on by default on a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-cmd
Print the equivalent command line and exit.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Never prompt; skip the menu.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
While the countdown is running:
.BR s
send now,
.BR p
pause or resume,
.BR +
and
.BR \-
shift the next wake by five minutes,
.BR q
quit. Ctrl\-C exits cleanly and reports how many wakes were delivered.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/claude\-waker/config
or
.IR ~/.config/claude\-waker/config .
Simple
.I key = value
lines, with optional
.BI [profile: name ]
sections selected by
.BR \-p .
Profiles layer on top of the top\-level keys.
.PP
Precedence is flags, then profile, then top\-level config, then built\-in
defaults. The file is parsed against a whitelist of known keys; it is never
sourced or evaluated, so it cannot execute code.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
iTerm2 is not running.
.TP
.B 4
Nothing matched, or a guard stopped the run.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Reproduce the original loop, with the sleep bug fixed:
.B claude\-waker run
.TP
Every session that is not mid\-answer, indefinitely:
.B claude\-waker run \-a \-\-if\-idle \-\-forever \-e 30m
.TP
Rehearse without sending:
.B claude\-waker run \-m dev3 \-\-dry\-run
.TP
See what is out there:
.B claude\-waker list
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-waker/config
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/iTerm2/Scripts/Claude Waker.py
Installed by
.BR "claude\-waker install\-plugin" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osascript (1)
.PP
https://github.com/vali\-m/iterm2\-claude\-waker
